description: Clean Architecture layer rules for Java source
globs: src/main/java/**/*.java
alwaysApply: false
---

# Java layer conventions

## controller/
- Map Request DTO → Command; Response DTO ← domain result
- `@ReadOnlyTransaction` on GET; `@ReadWriteTransaction` on POST/PUT/DELETE
- No repository or JPA imports

## usecase/
- `@Component` classes with `execute(Command)` methods
- Inject `domain.repository.*` and `domain.port.*` only
- `@Transactional` on write flows that persist + outbox event
- `@Cacheable` / `@CacheEvict` on read/write as in existing user/order use cases

## domain/
- Plain Java entities, ports, events, exceptions — no Spring/JPA annotations
- Cacheable domain types implement `Serializable` if returned from `@Cacheable` use cases

## infrastructure/
- `data/entities/` + `data/repository/` — JPA + port implementations
- `outbox/` — EventPublisher adapter; `outbox/relay/` — scheduler/service
- `components/` — filters, KafkaProducerService, Redis
- `appConfig/` — `@Configuration`, `@ConfigurationProperties`
